  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance d&#x2019;urgence au profit de 2 000 m&#xe9;nages vuln&#xe9;rables en pr&#xe9;vention de la situation de famine dans le nord du Mali</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide food security and agricultural livelihoods assistance to internally displaced persons, returnees, refugees and host community members in Ansongo and Menaka. This FAO project provides agricultural kits containing seeds and tools, rehabilitates to provide access to fresh water, and distributes US$206,000 through cash and voucher assistance. The food security component of this project provides humanitarian assistance to 7,200 people, including 1,900 women, 900 men, 4,400 children, and including 90 persons with disabilities. The agricultural livelihood component of this project provides humanitarian assistance to 4,800 people, including 1,200 women, 600 men, 3,000 children, and including 60 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
